{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And place it outside the camp.</b> It is divided into three parts: one he places on the Mount of Anointment, one is distributed to all the watches, and one he places in the חֵיל (Sifrei; Parah 3). The one for the watches was outside the Temple courtyard, for the people of the towns and all who need purification to take from it. The one on the Mount of Anointment — high priests consecrate other heifers from it. And the one in the חֵיל is given as a מִשְׁמֶרֶת by decree of Scripture, as it says <b>and it shall be for the congregation of the children of Israel לְמִשְׁמֶרֶת</b>." "<b>The water of sprinkling.</b> The water of sprinkling, as in ״וַיַּדּוּ אֶבֶן בִּי״ (Lamentations 3), ״לְיַדּוֹת אֶת קַרְנוֹת הַגּוֹיִם״ (Zechariah 2) — a term of sprinkling." "<b>It is a sin-offering.</b> A term of purification, as its plain sense. And according to its laws Scripture calls it חַטָּאת, to say that it is like consecrated offerings, forbidden for personal benefit (cf. Sifrei; Menachot 51)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:39.284238443Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}